   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Indefinites with singular versus plural",
     "texto": [
      "**Ogni** (each) and **qualche** (some) must be used with **singular** nouns: **ogni giorno** (every day), **qualche volta** (sometimes).",
      "By contrast, **alcuni / alcune** (some) always go with **plural** nouns: **alcuni turisti**, **alcune amiche**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Negation and totality",
     "texto": [
      "**Niente** (nothing) and **nessuno** (nobody / none) require a double negative when they come after the verb: **Non c'è niente** (there's nothing); **Non vedo nessuno** (I don't see anyone).",
      "**Tutto/a/i/e** agrees with the noun and usually takes an article before definite nouns: **tutti i giorni** (every day), **tutta la città** (the whole city)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
